# Side-effect hooks retain generated SMW collision. SMWDisX 3390ee1 bank_00
# HandlePlayerPhysics ($D5F2) reads native gameplay input before reaching the
# later UpdatePlayerSpritePosition ($DC2D) velocity seam. The early hook owns
# pad suppression; DC2D commits velocity, then HandlePlayerLevelCollision
# ($E92B), then PlayerState00_00CD24's inline $CD36 block joins ordinary
# flow. The CD36 standalone entry is an external-only dispatch target; the
# function-scoped block patch in apply_overrides.py owns the live seam.
# ProcessNormalSprites begins at $01:808C; its first generated M1X1 entry at
# $01:80D2 is the later carry bridge seam. Restrict M1X1.
@hook HandlePlayerPhysics -> SmwFalconBeforePlayerPhysics M1X1
@hook UpdatePlayerSpritePosition -> SmwFalconBeforePhysics M1X1
@hook ProcessNormalSprites_GetNormalSpriteOAMIndexAndDecrementTimers -> SmwFalconBeforeNormalSprites M1X1
@hook Spr035_Yoshi -> SmwFalconBeforeYoshi M1X1
